    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Cancer presents a formidable and growing challenge across Africa, where healthcare systems grapple with a unique constellation of epidemics. Dr Miriam Mutebi, Assistant Professor at the Aga Khan University (AKU) and President of the African Organisation for Research and Training in Cancer (AORTIC), is at the forefront of a global effort to address this crisis. As part of an  expert group  appointed by the World Bank, Dr Mutebi is providing a critical African perspective to a major strategic review of global cancer.",
